\tag{fdip}
\title{Reference constructions for discrete induction}
\date{2026-10-30}

\p{Fields on finite carriers, pairings and split maps give the algebraic
prerequisites for Gaussian induction. Observable functionals and
reference measures then specify what integration preserves.
Positive and constrained laws, background symmetries, group-algebra
sectors and spatial Dirac operators develop these constructions with
their own hypotheses.}

\p{The [main discussion](fdip-0001) uses these prerequisites for
[retained observables](fdip-0018),
[enriched-background comparisons](fdip-001E),
[configuration Clifford algebras](fdip-001B) and
[arithmetic families](fdip-001D).
[Further constructions and examples](fdip-0040) give complementary
operator and finite-state results.}

